// FILE: module_law_v1.law
/*******************************************************************************
 *                           AVIS.ARTIFACT HEADER
 * TYPE: LAW
 * CLASS: MODULE-LAW
 * NAME: MODULE-LAW-V1
 * VERSION: 1.00
 * ROLE: Behavioral Rules for System Modules
 * ENGINE: AVIS-2026 / AIFVS-MODE
 * ORIGIN: /mercwar01/law/module_law_v1.law
 *******************************************************************************
 * [PURPOSE]
 * Define how modules behave, interact, and expose functionality within the
 * AVIS ecosystem.
 *
 * [MODULE PRINCIPLES]
 * 1. Single Responsibility:
 *    Each module must focus on one domain or function.
 *
 * 2. Clear Interfaces:
 *    Modules must expose well-defined inputs and outputs.
 *
 * 3. Encapsulation:
 *    Internal logic should not be exposed unless required.
 *
 * 4. Predictability:
 *    Module behavior must remain stable across versions.
 *
 * [MODULE STRUCTURE]
 * Each module must include:
 *   - NAME
 *   - PURPOSE
 *   - INPUTS
 *   - OUTPUTS
 *   - DEPENDENCIES
 *
 * [INTERACTION RULES]
 * - Modules communicate only through defined interfaces.
 * - No module may modify another module’s state directly.
 *
 * [EXTENSION RULES]
 * - New features must not break existing interfaces.
 *
 * [COMPLIANCE]
 * All modules must follow this law to ensure system stability.
 *******************************************************************************
 * [END AVIS.ARTIFACT]
 *******************************************************************************/
